    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="52.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 52.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="52.1" corresp="#wit-i">E si il s'ent fuist dedenz la chalange, li sire rende sun were.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i">And if he escapes while he is under the accusation, the lord shall pay his wergeld.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="520"><ref target="clause:IICn_31-1">II Cn 31.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 31, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 274–275 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
